h":"apps/crq-python/docs/multi-repo.md","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Review the new history after a divergence."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"2343e0df2c1aac65c5bb3ba4063aa8f07db5de25","body":"**Do not skip post-floor commits on a new branch.**\n\nIf every branch commit is newer than `floor`, this initializes `reviewed_tip` to the current tip. All commits between the floor and the first tick are then permanently excluded from review. Use an empty-tree boundary or equivalent sentinel so those commits are reviewed.","id":"d32791d501a508f572fb7a69f791e55bd6ca79a218a7ab00d048aa1cbc8e6dd7","intervals":[],"path":"apps/crq-python/docs/multi-repo.md","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Do not skip post-floor commits on a new branch."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"2343e0df2c1aac65c5bb3ba4063aa8f07db5de25","body":"**Apply PR ranks before the repository tier.**\n\nThis rule assigns foreign-repository open PRs and follow-ups `rank_tier` before checking their kinds. They receive rank 2–4 instead of the ranks 0 and 1 promised at `apps/crq-python/docs/multi-repo.md:43-45`. They can wait behind primary post-merge work and starve under sustained load. Check PR kinds before applying the repository tier.","id":"31793714c1a9c58e06af5b0bd968a84c6f62ae7103a8c765a810b0aa3806067a","intervals":[],"path":"apps/crq-python/docs/multi-repo.md","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Apply PR ranks before the repository tier."}],"head":"33dac95cfce38928a05df549521759044f895a14","head_tree":"5a2179fb215610b97f73524380c02df5f0105de8","input_scope":[{"blob":"2343e0df2c1aac65c5bb3ba4063aa8f07db5de25","intervals":[[1,214]],"path":"apps/crq-python/docs/multi-repo.md"}],"job_id":"fd4c4e79627f60b0cdcdc8459162fe71c938196f2caba1555c44b2af529b4232:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"2343e0df2c1aac65c5bb3ba4063aa8f07db5de25","disposi